sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as ODH Dashboard<br/>(Gen AI Studio)
    participant KServe as KServe<br/>(llmisvc-controller)
    participant StorageInit as storage-initializer<br/>(Init Container)
    participant vLLM as vLLM<br/>(Model Server)
    participant EPP as llm-d Router (EPP)<br/>(Cache-aware Routing)
    participant EnvoyGW as Envoy Gateway<br/>(data-science-gateway)
    participant Client as External Client

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 1: LLM Model Deployment and Serving

    User->>Dashboard: Create LLMInferenceService<br/>via Gen AI Studio UI
    Dashboard->>KServe: Submit LLMISvc CR<br/>(HTTPS, SA token)
    KServe->>KServe: Reconcile LLMISvc CR
    KServe->>KServe: Create Deployment,<br/>InferencePool, HTTPRoute,<br/>LeaderWorkerSet

    Note over StorageInit: Init container phase
    StorageInit->>StorageInit: Download model from<br/>S3/HuggingFace/PVC<br/>(HTTPS, AWS IAM)

    Note over vLLM: Model server starts
    vLLM->>vLLM: Load model, expose<br/>OpenAI-compatible API
    vLLM->>EPP: Report Prometheus metrics<br/>(KV cache, queue depth)
    EPP->>EPP: Scrape metrics,<br/>cache-aware endpoint selection

    Note over Client,EnvoyGW: Production inference
    Client->>EnvoyGW: POST /v1/completions<br/>(HTTPS/443, TLS)
    EnvoyGW->>EPP: ext_proc: pick endpoint<br/>(Filter-Score-Pick)
    EPP-->>EnvoyGW: Selected vLLM pod endpoint
    EnvoyGW->>vLLM: Forward request<br/>(HTTP, InferencePool routing)
    vLLM-->>EnvoyGW: Streaming response
    EnvoyGW-->>Client: JSON/SSE response<br/>(HTTPS)

    User->>Dashboard: View model metrics
    Dashboard->>KServe: Query model status<br/>(K8s API)
    Dashboard-->>User: Show serving status<br/>and performance metrics

